When users want to claim their withdraw, claim() function will transfer the related funds to users. The vulnerability is that we use `transfer()` to transfer ETHER. If the user is one contract, and there are some logic in their fallback function, the claim may be failed because of out of gas. If user's contract cannot be upgraded, users' funds will be stuck in WithdrawQueue contract.

